      "writtenOn": "2026-10-19T09:59:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think SPDM.Requester and the action are added here before Type and Enabled are known, so a TPM or disabled resource would get them as well. The schema says SPDM should only be there when the type is SPDM and ComponentIntegrityEnabled is true, and the action only for SPDM. Would it work to set them in fillComponentIntegrityProperties, after Type and Enabled are read?",
      "revId": "351c6fc221d473b7ce2b6681db24f20e1ad937a7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "866f9790_60310e64",
        "filename": "redfish-core/lib/component_integrity.hpp",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 337,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002796
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-19T18:09:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. The SPDM object (Requester and IdentityAuthentication) is added only when Type is SPDM and ComponentIntegrityEnabled is true. IdentityAuthentication is now read after the ComponentIntegrity properties, so a disabled or TPM resource gets neither. The action is added for Type SPDM only, which is what the schema requires for it.",
      "parentUuid": "3d62e10f_4c6e20ae",
      "revId": "351c6fc221d473b7ce2b6681db24f20e1ad937a7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
