        "id": 1003181
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-19T09:59:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When spdmd rejects the request with xyz.openbmc_project.Common.Error.InvalidArgument (for eg short nonce or empty certificate slot) this returns 500. Since MeasurementSet declares InvalidArgument for bad input, I think it would be better to return a 400 for that case and keep 500 for InternalFailure. Would that be okay?",
      "revId": "351c6fc221d473b7ce2b6681db24f20e1ad937a7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52b2f879_9a16d757",
        "filename": "redfish-core/lib/component_integrity.hpp",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 451,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002796
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-19T18:09:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that InvalidArgument should be a 400. Which Redfish message would you like for it? spdmd\u0027s error doesn\u0027t say which parameter it rejected, and bmcweb now checks the Nonce format and the SlotId range before the call, so I\u0027d rather follow your preference than guess at a parameter name. I\u0027ll add it in the next patchset.",
      "parentUuid": "a345d125_9cafdce9",
      "revId": "351c6fc221d473b7ce2b6681db24f20e1ad937a7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
